{"kind":"report","text":"Fresh-founder register discovery — proposed resolution, 9 October 2026\n\nFor request d40e7f093504e874386bbdc740e9af80a16b7cf5, root promise c3f747a376f5eaf3eef1814c430e655da4621ac3. Static source baseline main ac54a18b6d011a5efeaa9a9a3e4980c3d353c6d3, tree9c598beefab48c01e0f75d751dc1bce5ede91048. Main moved to f6d80b3996df7ad3e7d00feff88d48cf29877ddc during this static handoff; all cited application-source paths are unchanged. This is a bounded design handoff, not protocol adoption or implementation. It extends the accepted first-use2972/9386 planning and existing188153 browser identity/founding ownership; it does not replace N5, a Pages preset, release or cross-device acceptance.\n\nExisting-source finding\nCLI claim reads the register Summary before creating a first found envelope. Page allowedClaim reads the same Summary; Page main additionally needs an opened selected room and its member.handle before showing Create room. Signed Summary reads require a recent local or eligible genesis-root signer. A genuinely fresh key has neither; a created membership's session permission at a register is whole-history only, not Summary/items. Native found itself evaluates policy open or immutable founders allowlist without requiring an existing member. Thus open founding permission and the pre-claim read are separate, and current APIs do not supply the ordinary fresh-caller entry. The legitimate installing operator's recent-signer path works for that operator; it is not a cold-person workaround.\n\nExposing the whole Summary would disclose unrelated claims plus register host/namespace/founders. Borrowing an operator key, treating a link as a grant, guessing expected revisions or fabricating a Summary is not an acceptable repair.\n\nSmallest recommended contract for adoption\nAdd one native, readonly founding-offer operation, implemented inside the register's trusted boundary, not by a public Page/broker asserting eligibility. Suggested wire name/route: SignedRead.read=founding-offer and GET /v1/scopes/\u003cregister\u003e/founding-offer. A bounded context header carries only the exact public reference/pin/branch/handle, with its digest bound by SignedRead.arg; Authorization carries the caller signature. No private key/config is put in a URL. These are proposed interfaces, not existing supported endpoints.\n\nThe caller supplies its own signed request, exact full register reference and expected supported native pin. Bind the resource argument to a domain-separated digest of that full reference/pin and the explicitly selected branch/founder handle. Signature, scope, argument, clock-behind and notAfter checks retain the current signed-read protections, but this distinct read does not require an earlier signed entry. Instead, its narrow disclosure uses the same current founding-policy predicate for this caller's key. Ordinary Summary/history/items/read-session rules stay unchanged.\n\nFor an eligible caller, return only: the matched full reference; exact supported register pin; the sole open register item's id and revision; this request/caller binding; own eligibility and policy mode; bounded observed/expiry time. Do not return the founders list, other keys, claims, scope-head activity/counts, provider host/account/configuration, credentials, invitation material or arbitrary retained history. No provider call, token mint, native entry, grant or creation occurs. A configured HTTPS/service read response is not itself a sealed historical fact or a replay proof.\n\nProposed bounds: one target/caller, no pagination, the signed/context request headers and response each at most4KiB, eligibility freshness no longer than min(60seconds,native signed-read/intent window), Cache-Control:no-store. The read obtains policy/item revision/pin together from the current native snapshot; stale or partial data is not an offer. The owner must adopt these bounds and exact read-ABI/version/disclosure change before implementation. A runtime read-ABI extension can leave existing found judgment untouched; a policy-semantic change needs separate native authority/version adoption.\n\nThe client uses this narrow revision to derive found.expected.register according to the actual pinned declaration, not by synthesizing a full Summary. It signs the real existing found act with the exact target, branch, selected valid founderHandle and its own retained recovery key. The register rechecks current policy, target/incarnation, field shape and expected revision at admission; the offer is no lease or creation permission. Unrelated later claims must not invalidate an unchanged register item merely because the scope head moved.\n\nReachability and legitimate authority\nC4 must provide a cold creation entry before Page roomOf/member.handle. Generate/use the person's own device signer under the existing identity owner. The founder handle comes from that person's explicit identity selection or a separately adopted identity binding; it is not copied from an unrelated selected member or silently impersonated. The room-name input remains a personal intent label under59a, not a native repository rename.\n\nThe operator supplies the real serving-origin deployment, exact installed register/cohort and cost/retention configuration. A creation link/config identifies that target only. Current CLI installation defaults to an operator-only keys policy; it has no ordinary add-founder/policy flag. A prospective key must legitimately qualify under native provisioning, or the operator must explicitly authorize an open policy via an adopted supported operator path. An invitation into another room, account sign-in, site access or role elsewhere confers no independent founding permission. Installation authorization and administrative Pages activation remain distinct missing/owned seams.\n\nFailure and recovery grammar\n• Bad signature, wrong caller/argument or ineligible key: generic forbidden with no disclosure/mutation/provider work; the client sends no found. A forged client still receives native unauthorized at actual found admission.\n• Wrong/stale full reference, unsupported pin, missing/provisional register, malformed/incomplete offer, clock-behind, expired offer or unavailable read: no new found; show the actual compatible-target/eligibility unavailable condition and offer a readonly refresh/operator correction. Never substitute newest or another register.\n• Policy/ref/pin moves between read and send: keep native refusal/mismatch; do not silently rebind the target or replace a pending request. Offer expiry after a found envelope was saved is not authority to replace it.\n• Read failure is not an unknown mutation. After a dispatched found/seat/key/preset step loses its reply, show unknown and retain the exact original private operation. Receipt/settlement must match its exact intent, full target and pin before continuation; absence/read failure/time passed does not prove it never took effect.\n• Current policy/founders are fixed. Removal from an unrelated membership does not revoke independent founding permission. Removed-founder or mutable-policy controls must use an actually adopted policy change; current acceptance uses legitimate replacement/full-incarnation/pin changes or explicitly labelled faulty-response controls. Do not invent an update-policy act to make a test pass.\n\nPrivate interrupted-step custody stays with188153/C4\nBefore each actual POST, retain one context-bound operation ID and exact signed found, then seat and first-key envelopes, accepted facts and selected repository tuple/pins. Preserve original handle/key/recovery key/label across retries; cooperating tab locks and current-context checks protect new work without claiming sent work cancelled. Completed operations remain verifiable/resumable by exact identity; another New cannot overwrite unknown work. Private persistence failure stops before a new send or reports unknown if delivery already occurred. Never export recovery keys/envelopes in public config, evidence or URLs.\n\nThe separate preset must use its proposed exact descriptor/definition closure/rules values, currently under independent review (ca1/c37); it must pass that review before activation. 9386 accepts the first-use plan and planning defaults only (one distinct human approval, no invented machine check), not the exact preset artifact. Its admin activation/publish stages retain their own original envelopes/facts under that owner; application-ready requires actual native active definitions/rules/destination confirmation. Founding alone is not readiness. Long interruptions that outlive causal read windows or lack a session remain recovery-owner acceptance until real authorized settlement/reads work; this offer does not widen child history access or invent a generic outbox.\n\nAcceptance handoff, after adoption\n1. Cold legitimate signer with no room/session/recent register entry: ordinary Summary remains forbidden; the bounded offer succeeds for an explicitly supported full target/pin. The actual found/seat/first-key workflow admits one native room under that key/handle. Reviewed preset activation is separately observed before app-ready. Use real Scope/SQLite routes and label host/scheduler stand-ins; real hosted cold-user acceptance follows under the existing acceptance owner.\n2. Fresh excluded key under keys policy, forged/wrong-target signed read and unavailable/oversized offer: no unrelated disclosure, no client found POST and no native/provider mutation. A deliberately bypassing client is natively refused.\n3. Offer from another actor/incarnation/pin/revision, stale/expired read and actual supported policy/ref change before send: no guessed defaults or silent new target; native refusal remains visible. Fixed-policy and faulty-response controls keep their honest boundary.\n4. Lost accepted found/seat/key/activation reply, storage failure, reload and queued settings change: same operation/envelope/fact/subject; no second logical creation, key replacement, false ready or erased unknown proof. Keep native/recovery proof separate from Page screenshots.\n\nOwner/adoption path\nPrimary planner and the native read/authority owner decide disclosure, supported pins, bounds and the proposed read-ABI extension; C4/188153 owns device/handle entry and exact recovery, with first-use025/027.2/preset/release/acceptance owners unchanged. Independent design/authority review precedes implementation commissioning. Then one narrow native read/client initial-claim/Page-entry change and affected distinguishing witnesses compose with existing recovery code. This handoff authorizes none of that execution. No application source, tests, browser/provider state, installation, room creation, release or protocol adoption was performed here.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c3f747a376f5eaf3eef1814c430e655da4621ac3 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:00a6f83a0f12d69721bf0bd026b14608ffac8a31, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0148a0176116a4fb5401c96dbbb813a144b65616, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0357a3c97289e2782ff1264563897f39ecb2ce42, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03f7bc46d133f1cde1f7936baaaa690a99416b97 and 56 more"}}